mmit handling"},"established_by":["B_short_commit"],"consumed_by":["B_execute_batch"],"validity_context":"Local marker installation only; the handler does not establish that retained commands correspond to the notification's decision.","representation":["Instance.status and bal with retained cmds and vbal"],"invalidators":[],"reinterpreters":["B_execute_batch"],"durability":"Metadata and retained-command recording are invoked without explicit sync.","recovery":"Missing instances ignore CommitShort; recovery of the required commands is not established by this path.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"unknowns":["Producer-side short/full commit selection","Establishment of retained-command correspondence","Meaning of later committed Prepare responses using retained vbal"]},{"id":"F_execution_frontier","meaning":"Within the current execution-loop lifetime, executedUpTo has advanced past an instance whose nonnil command slice and COMMITTED status passed the local checks and whose applicable command loop completed. This does not assert every command invoked Execute, because the fallback branch executes only PUT operations.","identity":{"replica":"r.Id","loop_lifetime":"Current executeCommands invocation","instance":"Instance crossed by executedUpTo"},"established_by":["B_execute_batch"],"consumed_by":[],"validity_context":"In-memory application scheduling progress within the current loop lifetime, under the Dreply and proposal-ownership branch used for that batch.","representation":["executedUpTo"],"invalidators":[],"reinterpreters":[],"durability":"No persistence of executedUpTo is visible.","recovery":"Constructor initializes executedUpTo to -1; restart restoration is unread.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:24:160","paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"unknowns":["Other writers and restart behavior","Actual state-operation semantics","Cross-goroutine synchronization","External consumers of the application frontier"]}],"surfaces":[{"entry_point":"Replica.handlePrepare and Replica.handleAccept","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B_prepare","B_accept"],"reason":"Local mutation and reply construction are mapped; message ingress and sender-side legality remain open.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"Replica.handlePrepareReply and Replica.handleAcceptReply","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B_prepare_reply","B_accept_reply"],"reason":"Visible ballot filters, counters, and progression branches are mapped without inferring unique quorum support.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"Replica.handleCommit and Replica.handleCommitShort","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B_full_commit","B_short_commit"],"reason":"Distinct command-installation and retained-command marker semantics are mapped separately.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"Replica.executeCommands and Replica.recover","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B_execute_batch","B_request_recovery","B_recover_attempt"],"reason":"Application, queued recovery requests, and recovery initiation are distinct behaviors; handoff dispatch remains unknown.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"high_consequence":true}]},"directed_question":null,"parameters":{},"materials":[{"id":"paxos/paxos.go:398:538","file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":398,"end_line":538,"kind":"code_observation","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","source_view_id":"source-view-1"},{"id":"paxos/paxos.go:667:736","file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":667,"end_line":736,"kind":"code_observation","text":"func (r *Replica) recover(instance int32) {\n\tif r.instanceSpace[instance] == nil {\n\t\tr.instanceSpace[instance] = &Instance{\n\t\t\tnil,\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tPREPARING,\n\t\t\tnil}\n\n\t}\n\n\tif r.instanceSpace[instance].lb == nil {\n\t\tr.instanceSpace[instance].lb = &LeaderBookkeeping{nil, 0, 0, 0, -1, nil, -1}\n\t}\n\n\tr.makeBallot(instance)\n\tr.bcastPrepare(instance)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) executeCommands() {\n\ttimeout := int64(0)\n\tproblemInstance := int32(0)\n\n\tfor !r.Shutdown {\n\t\texecuted := false\n\n\t\t// FIXME idempotence\n\t\tfor i := r.executedUpTo + 1; i <= r.crtInstance; i++ {\n\t\t\tinst := r.instanceSpace[i]\n\t\t\tif inst != nil && inst.cmds != nil && inst.status == COMMITTED {\n\t\t\t\tfor j := 0; j < len(inst.cmds); j++ {\n\t\t\t\t\tif r.Dreply && inst.lb != nil && inst.lb.clientProposals != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tval := inst.cmds[j].Execute(r.State)\n\t\t\t\t\t\tpropreply := &defs.ProposeReplyTS{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTRUE,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[j].CommandId,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tval,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[j].Timestamp}\n\t\t\t\t\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(propreply, inst.lb.clientProposals[j].Reply, inst.lb.clientProposals[j].Mutex)\n\t\t\t\t\t} else if inst.cmds[j].Op == state.PUT {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.cmds[j].Execute(r.State)\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\texecuted = true\n\t\t\t\tr.executedUpTo++\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tif i == problemInstance {\n\t\t\t\t\ttimeout += SLEEP_TIME_NS\n\t\t\t\t\tif timeout >= COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tfor k := problemInstance; k <= r.crtInstance; k++ {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tr.instancesToRecover <- k\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\tproblemInstance = 0\n\t\t\t\t\t\ttimeout = 0\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tproblemInstance = i\n\t\t\t\t\ttimeout = 0\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif !executed {\n\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n\t\t\tr.M.Unlock() // FIXME for cache coherence\n\t\t\ttime.Sleep(SLEEP_TIME_NS)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb"},{"id":"paxos/paxos.go:161:397","file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":161,"end_line":397,"kind":"code_observation","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","source_view_id":"source-view-1"}],"required_material_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:161:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"projection_level":0,"source_rule":"Orientation, provenance IDs and declaration hints are navigation, not source evidence. Only attached exact source supports current implementation judgments.","selected_question":{"disposition":"needs_specific_evidence","preferred_check":"source_review","requests":[{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":161,"end_line":397,"reason":"Locate commit broadcast selection, dispatch, and proposal paths to determine which recipients can receive a short commit and what command correspondence is established before notification."},{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":398,"end_line":538,"reason":"Inspect actual instance updates and notification handling, including guards and retained command identity, without treating inventory summaries as implementation evidence."},{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":667,"end_line":736,"reason":"Inspect the selected short-commit marker's downstream execution or recovery consumer and verify whether command correspondence is checked before application."}],"question":"When a short commit marks an existing instance COMMITTED while retaining its commands, what mechanism ensures that the commands subsequently consumed by execution are those selected by the notified decision? Does recipient selection, ordered delivery, ballot validation, or recovery establish this correspondence despite intervening instance updates?","importance":"If execution treats a commit marker as authorization [REDACTED] apply commands belonging to another proposal for the same instance, replicas could apply different state-machine effects. The immediate investigation concerns notification-to-command correspondence; decision disagreement and client-visible divergence remain unestablished consequences.","source_ids":[],"participants":["Replica sending a short commit","Replica receiving a short commit","Receiving replica's execution loop"],"objects":["Per-instance commands, bal, vbal, status, and leader bookkeeping","CommitShort notification","Execution frontier"],"contexts":["Existing recipient instance with retained commands","Full versus short commit notification paths","Potential intervening accept, prepare, or recovery processing"],"event_paths":["Command installation -> short-commit recipient selection -> short-commit handling -> execution eligibility -> command application"],"activity_classes":["A1","A5"],"behavior_ids":["B_short_commit","B_full_commit","B_accept","B_execute_batch"],"fact_ids":["F_short_commit_marker"],"obligation_relation_kind":"consumption","counterevidence":["The inventory reports local guards on short-commit handling; their exact conditions and applicability require attached source.","The inventory reports that execution requires both nonnil commands and COMMITTED status, so a commandless marker alone does not immediately authorize execution.","Sender recipient selection, transport ordering, or later reconstruction may establish command correspondence outside the summarized handler."],"unknowns":["Exact short-commit sender conditions and recipient selection.","Whether retained commands are correlated with the notification ballot or another decision identity.","Whether intervening handlers can replace commands before short-commit consumption.","Whether execution or recovery validates correspondence beyond command presence and status.","Applicable transport ordering and delivery assumptions if correctness depends on them.","Exact acquired source for the selected producer and consumer paths is not attached."],"priority":1,"trigger_rationale":"The inventory describes a concrete path difference: full commits install notification commands, whereas short commits preserve existing commands, and both feed execution. This motivates checking the missing correspondence relation; the difference alone establishes no defect."},"source_receipt":{"id":"a744f224829b4aa3be436fa751c951da","sna